WEBVTT

00:00:08.147 --> 00:00:10.868
The Truth Machine by Norman Whitney.

00:00:10.928 --> 00:00:13.900
A Heinemann guided reader at beginner level.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.751
Copyright Heinemann International.

00:00:16.811 --> 00:00:18.432
First recorded 1982.

00:00:18.492 --> 00:00:24.644
This edition 1992.

00:00:24.704 --> 00:00:29.167
CHAPTER I.

00:00:29.227 --> 00:00:30.427
SUCCESS.

00:00:30.487 --> 00:00:32.638
THE PROFESSIVARITY.

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.439
SUCCESS.

00:00:34.499 --> 00:00:36.417
CRIDE PROFESSIVARITY.

00:00:36.477 --> 00:00:38.686
My new invention is ready.

00:00:38.746 --> 00:00:40.657
It is now complete.

00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:43.970
I shall call it the truth machine."

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:48.464
The professor ran to the telephone and phoned the newspaper office.

00:00:48.524 --> 00:00:50.865
He told them about the truth machine.

00:00:50.885 --> 00:00:54.868
"'Come to my laboratory,' he said.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:58.000
"'You will see my new invention.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:01.248
I call it the truth machine.'

00:01:01.308 --> 00:01:06.247
"'Please give us your name and address,' said the girl at the newspaper office.

00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:09.720
"'We'll send a reporter immediately.'

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:13.052
The professor gave the girl his name and address.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:17.986
"'Will the reporter be here soon?'

00:01:18.045 --> 00:01:18.816
he asked.

00:01:18.836 --> 00:01:22.078
"'Yes, of course,' replied the girl.

00:01:22.098 --> 00:01:26.092
"'Good,' said Professor Verity.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.672
He smiled.

00:01:27.732 --> 00:01:29.163
He waited.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:32.964
The reporter soon arrived at the laboratory.

00:01:33.024 --> 00:01:36.246
Who can use the truth machine, Professor?

00:01:36.306 --> 00:01:37.617
He asked.

00:01:37.677 --> 00:01:41.739
Anybody can use it, replied Professor Verity.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:46.282
But how does the machine work, asked the reporter?

00:01:46.342 --> 00:01:48.364
The professor laughed.

00:01:48.424 --> 00:01:51.316
That's a secret, he said.

00:01:51.376 --> 00:01:53.567
But I can tell you this.

00:01:53.627 --> 00:01:58.461
The questioner sits in the little chair, eyes sit at the controls.

00:01:58.521 --> 00:02:01.664
And the truth-speaker sits in the big chair.

00:02:01.724 --> 00:02:05.295
The truth-speaker always speaks the truth.

00:02:05.355 --> 00:02:07.616
He cannot tell lies.

00:02:07.676 --> 00:02:10.147
The professor smiled.

00:02:10.207 --> 00:02:13.078
Why did you make the truth machine?

00:02:13.138 --> 00:02:14.860
asked the reporter.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.531
I love truth, said Professor Verity.

00:02:18.591 --> 00:02:20.402
And I hate lies.

00:02:20.462 --> 00:02:24.374
I love good people, and I hate bad people.

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:27.417
I love peace, and I hate war.

00:02:27.477 --> 00:02:31.460
The truth machine loves truth, good people, and peace.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:35.821
It hates lies, bad people, and war."

00:02:35.881 --> 00:02:39.552
The reporter wrote all this in his notebook.

00:02:39.612 --> 00:02:44.754
Soon everybody will know about the truth machine, said the professor.

00:02:44.814 --> 00:02:47.275
It will be a success.

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:53.877
The reporter thanked the professor and hurried back to his newspaper office.

00:02:53.936 --> 00:02:57.111
Professor Verity was right.

00:02:57.171 --> 00:03:01.596
Soon millions of people knew about the truth machine.

00:03:01.656 --> 00:03:04.246
The professor was on the radio.

00:03:04.306 --> 00:03:06.496
He was on the television, too.

00:03:06.556 --> 00:03:14.238
All over the world, newspapers and magazines wrote about Professor Verity and the truth machine.

00:03:14.298 --> 00:03:17.428
Many people wrote to Professor Verity.

00:03:17.488 --> 00:03:24.020
Rich people, poor people, young people, old people, everybody sent letters.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.564
The truth machine was a success.

00:03:27.623 --> 00:03:30.738
Thank you, wrote one woman.

00:03:30.798 --> 00:03:33.789
Wonderful, wrote another.

00:03:33.849 --> 00:03:36.410
Good luck, wrote one man.

00:03:36.469 --> 00:03:38.300
I am sending you some money.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.350
It will help your work.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.852
Many people sent money.

00:03:42.912 --> 00:03:50.664
Some sent coins, others sent banknotes, and others sent checks and money orders.

00:03:50.724 --> 00:03:54.805
Then the professor chose his first clients.

00:03:54.865 --> 00:03:57.652
He read his letters many times.

00:03:57.712 --> 00:04:00.359
First he chose a hundred letters.

00:04:00.418 --> 00:04:02.800
Then he chose fifty of them.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.542
Then he chose ten names.

00:04:05.602 --> 00:04:09.156
Finally he chose three people.

00:04:09.216 --> 00:04:18.772
Mrs. Seeker, from Australia, Inspector Sack, from South America, and Dr. Simple from the United States.

00:04:18.832 --> 00:04:35.272
Professor Verity wrote to them, Please come and see me, he wrote, You will be one of my first clients.

00:04:35.332 --> 00:04:44.126
Chapter 2.

00:04:44.186 --> 00:04:48.288
Three visitors for Professor Verity.

00:04:48.347 --> 00:04:52.828
Two weeks later, Professor Verity had a visitor.

00:04:52.888 --> 00:04:54.739
It was Mrs. Seeker.

00:04:54.799 --> 00:04:56.650
She was from Australia.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.550
She was a housewife.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.730
She was afraid.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:03.411
Can I help you, Mrs. Seeker?

00:05:03.471 --> 00:05:05.162
Ask the professor.

00:05:05.222 --> 00:05:08.372
Yes, Mrs. Seeker replied.

00:05:08.432 --> 00:05:11.482
I wrote to you about the truth machine.

00:05:11.542 --> 00:05:14.204
I know, said the Professor.

00:05:14.264 --> 00:05:16.315
You will be my first client.

00:05:16.375 --> 00:05:18.117
Don't be afraid."

00:05:18.176 --> 00:05:20.638
I'll, said Mrs. Seeker.

00:05:20.698 --> 00:05:23.390
I will not be your first client, Professor.

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:26.352
Your first client will be my husband.

00:05:26.412 --> 00:05:29.844
Your husband, said Professor Verity.

00:05:29.904 --> 00:05:32.106
The Professor was surprised.

00:05:32.166 --> 00:05:35.148
But your husband didn't write to me.

00:05:35.208 --> 00:05:38.660
No, he didn't, said Mrs. Seeker.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.556
I wrote to you.

00:05:40.616 --> 00:05:42.712
But what do you want?"

00:05:42.772 --> 00:05:43.853
asked the professor.

00:05:43.873 --> 00:05:45.354
"'Why are you here?"

00:05:45.374 --> 00:05:48.837
"'Well,' said Mrs. Seeker.

00:05:48.857 --> 00:05:53.100
"'My husband,' Mrs. Seeker stopped.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:54.502
She was crying.

00:05:54.562 --> 00:05:55.642
She was unhappy.

00:05:55.662 --> 00:06:00.516
"'My husband,' Mrs. Seeker stopped again.

00:06:00.576 --> 00:06:01.987
She was crying again.

00:06:02.007 --> 00:06:06.131
"'Oh,' said the professor quietly.

00:06:06.151 --> 00:06:10.927
"'Your husband has another woman.

00:06:10.987 --> 00:06:14.972
Yes, yes, cried Mrs. Seeker.

00:06:15.032 --> 00:06:16.852
But I don't know.

00:06:16.912 --> 00:06:18.713
Oh, I hate lies.

00:06:18.773 --> 00:06:20.724
I want the truth, Professor.

00:06:20.784 --> 00:06:23.994
I want the truth from my husband.

00:06:24.054 --> 00:06:28.397
But will he come here, ask the Professor?

00:06:28.457 --> 00:06:30.598
Oh, yes, he'll come.

00:06:30.657 --> 00:06:32.478
Said Mrs. Seeker.

00:06:32.538 --> 00:06:37.170
Well, bring him to my laboratory, said the Professor.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.388
I'll help you, Mrs. Seeker.

00:06:39.448 --> 00:06:43.578
Of course, there will be a small charge, a fee.

00:06:43.638 --> 00:06:46.870
I'll pay anything," said Mrs. Seeker.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:48.401
I hate lies.

00:06:48.461 --> 00:06:51.042
I want the truth from my husband.

00:06:51.102 --> 00:06:55.124
Come here next Monday morning," said the professor.

00:06:55.184 --> 00:06:57.796
Everything will be ready.

00:06:57.856 --> 00:07:01.748
The next visitor was Inspector Sack.

00:07:01.808 --> 00:07:03.839
He was from South America.

00:07:03.899 --> 00:07:07.061
He was a policeman, and he had a gun.

00:07:07.121 --> 00:07:09.335
Hello, Professor!

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:11.069
said the Inspector.

00:07:11.129 --> 00:07:14.382
The Inspector had a loud voice.

00:07:14.442 --> 00:07:16.814
Where is it, Professor?

00:07:16.874 --> 00:07:17.954
He shouted.

00:07:18.014 --> 00:07:20.927
Where is the truth machine?

00:07:20.986 --> 00:07:25.810
It's here, Inspector, said Professor Verity quietly.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:29.062
You will be one of my first clients.

00:07:29.122 --> 00:07:32.986
All good, said the Inspector.

00:07:33.046 --> 00:07:36.118
Inspector Sack walked up and down.

00:07:36.178 --> 00:07:37.639
Then he stopped.

00:07:37.699 --> 00:07:39.800
He looked at the Professor.

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:43.152
Climb, shouted Inspector Sack.

00:07:43.212 --> 00:07:46.644
Climb, climb, climb.

00:07:46.704 --> 00:07:50.808
Climb, asked the professor in a soft voice.

00:07:50.868 --> 00:07:54.932
Yes, crime, shouted Inspector Sack.

00:07:54.992 --> 00:07:57.063
I hate criminals.

00:07:57.123 --> 00:07:59.384
Murderers are criminals.

00:07:59.444 --> 00:08:01.336
They kill people.

00:08:01.396 --> 00:08:03.512
I hate murderers.

00:08:03.571 --> 00:08:05.776
Thieves are criminals.

00:08:05.835 --> 00:08:08.246
They take things from people.

00:08:08.306 --> 00:08:10.187
I hate thieves.

00:08:10.247 --> 00:08:13.058
And liars are criminals.

00:08:13.118 --> 00:08:15.228
They tell lies.

00:08:15.288 --> 00:08:18.139
I hate lies, Professor.

00:08:18.199 --> 00:08:21.160
I hate all criminals.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:27.492
But the truth machine will fight criminals, said Professor Verity, quietly.

00:08:27.552 --> 00:08:30.540
There will be no more murderers and thieves.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:35.119
There will be no more lies and no more crime, Inspector.

00:08:35.179 --> 00:08:41.381
No more criminals and no more crime, shouted Inspector Sack.

00:08:41.442 --> 00:08:43.362
Excellent.

00:08:43.422 --> 00:08:48.034
Bring your criminals to me, Inspector, said the Professor.

00:08:48.094 --> 00:08:52.086
Of course, there will be a small charge, a fee.

00:08:52.146 --> 00:08:53.396
Money?

00:08:53.456 --> 00:08:55.246
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:08:55.306 --> 00:08:57.886
You shall have money, Professor.

00:08:57.946 --> 00:09:00.638
We are fighting crime, my friend.

00:09:00.698 --> 00:09:03.750
Of course you shall have money."

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:07.691
Thank you, Inspector, said Professor Verity.

00:09:07.751 --> 00:09:09.272
Thank you.

00:09:09.332 --> 00:09:12.174
Come here next Monday afternoon.

00:09:12.233 --> 00:09:14.294
Bring your criminals to me.

00:09:14.354 --> 00:09:17.586
Everything will be ready.

00:09:17.646 --> 00:09:21.218
Good morning, Professor Verity.

00:09:21.278 --> 00:09:23.700
My name is Dr. Simple.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:26.863
Dr. Simple was the third visitor.

00:09:26.924 --> 00:09:29.085
He was from the United States.

00:09:29.145 --> 00:09:31.176
He was a government official.

00:09:31.236 --> 00:09:33.898
He worked for the American government.

00:09:33.958 --> 00:09:37.720
Hello, Dr. Simple, said the professor.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:40.642
You will be one of my first clients.

00:09:40.702 --> 00:09:43.604
I know, said Dr. Simple.

00:09:43.664 --> 00:09:45.935
I will be your third client.

00:09:45.996 --> 00:09:50.183
The other two are Mrs. Seeker and Inspector Sack.

00:09:50.243 --> 00:09:53.050
Oh, said the professor.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:55.352
How do you know their names?

00:09:55.412 --> 00:09:58.174
Dr. Simple looked round.

00:09:58.234 --> 00:10:03.528
Spies, Professor Verity, said Dr. Simple quietly.

00:10:03.589 --> 00:10:05.368
Spies.

00:10:05.428 --> 00:10:09.008
Spies, asked Professor Verity.

00:10:09.068 --> 00:10:13.100
But Mrs. Seeker and Inspector Sack aren't spies.

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:17.731
Of course they are not spies, said Dr. Simple.

00:10:17.791 --> 00:10:19.322
He looked round.

00:10:19.382 --> 00:10:21.873
But I am.

00:10:21.932 --> 00:10:26.804
Oh, you are a spy, the Professor asked.

00:10:26.864 --> 00:10:29.805
Yes, said Dr. Simple.

00:10:29.865 --> 00:10:31.766
I'm a spy.

00:10:31.826 --> 00:10:33.576
He looked round.

00:10:33.636 --> 00:10:36.366
He was looking for enemy spies.

00:10:36.426 --> 00:10:40.507
I fight for peace," said Dr. Simple.

00:10:40.567 --> 00:10:42.988
Professor Verity smiled.

00:10:43.048 --> 00:10:47.020
Oh, I want peace too, the Professor said.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.902
I know, said Dr. Simple.

00:10:49.962 --> 00:10:51.322
He smiled.

00:10:51.382 --> 00:10:53.484
You will help me, Professor.

00:10:53.544 --> 00:10:55.985
We have caught an enemy spy.

00:10:56.045 --> 00:10:58.156
He will not tell the truth.

00:10:58.216 --> 00:11:00.077
I will bring him here.

00:11:00.137 --> 00:11:01.818
I will be the questioner.

00:11:01.878 --> 00:11:04.198
He will be the truth-speaker.

00:11:04.258 --> 00:11:06.878
Yes, said the Professor.

00:11:06.938 --> 00:11:08.720
Please bring him here.

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:13.474
Of course, Dr. Simple, there will be a small charge, a fee.

00:11:13.534 --> 00:11:15.556
Dr. Simple smiled.

00:11:15.616 --> 00:11:16.846
He looked round again.

00:11:16.866 --> 00:11:19.448
Of course, Professor.

00:11:19.508 --> 00:11:21.160
Here is some money.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:25.062
Dr. Simple gave the Professor a lot of money.

00:11:25.122 --> 00:11:28.756
Thank you, said the Professor quietly.

00:11:28.816 --> 00:11:30.838
He looked round too.

00:11:30.898 --> 00:11:34.261
Come here with your spy next Monday evening.

00:11:34.321 --> 00:11:43.406
Everything will be ready.

00:11:43.466 --> 00:11:59.563
Chapter 3 Monday A busy day for Professor Verity It was Monday morning.

00:11:59.623 --> 00:12:02.304
Mrs. Seeker came to the laboratory.

00:12:02.364 --> 00:12:04.648
Mr. Seeker came too.

00:12:04.708 --> 00:12:06.670
How I, Professor?"

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:08.340
said Mr. Seeker.

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:12.211
Where is your trophy machine?

00:12:12.271 --> 00:12:14.362
Mr. Seeker laughed.

00:12:14.422 --> 00:12:17.412
Don't laugh, said his wife.

00:12:17.472 --> 00:12:19.032
She was afraid.

00:12:19.092 --> 00:12:21.223
Listen to the Professor.

00:12:21.283 --> 00:12:23.913
Professor Verity spoke.

00:12:23.973 --> 00:12:27.394
Mrs. Seeker, you are the questioner.

00:12:27.454 --> 00:12:29.514
Sit in the small chair.

00:12:29.574 --> 00:12:32.985
Mr. Seeker, you are the truth speaker.

00:12:33.045 --> 00:12:35.296
Sit in the big chair.

00:12:35.356 --> 00:12:39.018
Mr. and Mrs. Seeker sat in their chairs.

00:12:39.078 --> 00:12:42.069
Mrs. Seeker looked at the professor.

00:12:42.129 --> 00:12:44.260
What shall I say?

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:45.840
She asked.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:50.682
Ask your husband some easy questions, said the professor.

00:12:50.742 --> 00:12:53.132
She looked at her husband.

00:12:53.192 --> 00:12:55.353
What is your name?

00:12:55.413 --> 00:12:56.864
She asked.

00:12:56.924 --> 00:13:00.435
My name is Henry, said her husband.

00:13:00.495 --> 00:13:02.846
That was an easy question.

00:13:02.906 --> 00:13:04.613
He laughed.

00:13:04.672 --> 00:13:07.300
How old are you, Henry?"

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:09.232
asked Mrs. Seeker.

00:13:09.292 --> 00:13:13.133
I'm 47.

00:13:13.193 --> 00:13:15.835
Said Mr. Seeker.

00:13:15.895 --> 00:13:18.876
Mrs. Seeker looked at Professor Verity.

00:13:18.936 --> 00:13:20.298
She smiled.

00:13:20.358 --> 00:13:22.879
That's the truth, she said.

00:13:22.939 --> 00:13:25.870
He usually says 43.

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:29.823
My husband is telling the truth.

00:13:29.883 --> 00:13:34.168
Good, said Professor Verity.

00:13:34.228 --> 00:13:38.133
Now asked your husband some difficult questions.

00:13:38.193 --> 00:13:42.794
Mrs. Seeker was afraid, but she spoke.

00:13:42.854 --> 00:13:45.045
Are you married?

00:13:45.105 --> 00:13:46.475
She asked.

00:13:46.535 --> 00:13:50.246
Of course I'm married, replied Mr. Seeker.

00:13:50.306 --> 00:13:51.947
You're my wife.

00:13:52.007 --> 00:13:53.868
He was angry.

00:13:53.928 --> 00:13:58.389
But, but do you love me?

00:13:58.449 --> 00:14:00.549
Asked Mrs. Seeker.

00:14:00.609 --> 00:14:03.448
Mr. Seeker looked at his wife.

00:14:03.508 --> 00:14:05.596
She waited.

00:14:05.656 --> 00:14:07.458
No.

00:14:07.518 --> 00:14:09.589
He said slowly.

00:14:09.648 --> 00:14:11.089
No.

00:14:11.149 --> 00:14:12.860
I don't love you.

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:15.372
I'll have another woman.

00:14:15.432 --> 00:14:18.662
Oh, said Mrs. Seeker.

00:14:18.722 --> 00:14:20.423
Who do you love?

00:14:20.483 --> 00:14:21.854
Tell me the truth.

00:14:21.914 --> 00:14:23.114
I hate lies.

00:14:23.174 --> 00:14:24.785
Who do you love?

00:14:24.845 --> 00:14:27.246
Mrs. Seeker was crying.

00:14:27.306 --> 00:14:30.298
Mr. Seeker looked at his wife.

00:14:30.358 --> 00:14:33.384
I love anelyate.

00:14:33.444 --> 00:14:37.142
I love Ann Elliot, he said.

00:14:37.202 --> 00:14:38.984
Oh!

00:14:39.044 --> 00:14:40.654
Ann Elliot!

00:14:40.714 --> 00:14:43.537
But she's my best friend!

00:14:43.597 --> 00:14:46.099
Now you know the truth.

00:14:46.159 --> 00:14:49.692
Yes, that's the truth.

00:14:49.752 --> 00:14:54.435
What shall I do now?

00:14:54.496 --> 00:15:01.246
Inspector Sack came to the laboratory on Monday afternoon.

00:15:01.306 --> 00:15:04.504
His boss, the Chief Inspector, came too.

00:15:04.564 --> 00:15:07.886
They brought some criminals with them.

00:15:07.946 --> 00:15:10.928
Good afternoon, Professor!

00:15:10.988 --> 00:15:12.959
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:15:13.019 --> 00:15:16.061
This is my boss, the Chief Inspector.

00:15:16.121 --> 00:15:18.082
And these are the criminals.

00:15:18.142 --> 00:15:19.893
They are murderers.

00:15:19.953 --> 00:15:21.424
They are thieves.

00:15:21.484 --> 00:15:23.626
And they are liars.

00:15:23.686 --> 00:15:29.378
But today, said Professor Verity, they will tell the truth.

00:15:29.438 --> 00:15:31.328
Shall we begin?

00:15:31.388 --> 00:15:34.218
said the Chief Inspector quietly.

00:15:34.278 --> 00:15:36.589
Yes, let's begin.

00:15:36.649 --> 00:15:37.630
Come on.

00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:39.751
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:15:39.811 --> 00:15:43.103
Inspector Sack sat in the questioner's chair.

00:15:43.163 --> 00:15:46.665
The first criminal sat in the Truthspeaker's chair.

00:15:46.725 --> 00:15:48.956
Inspector Sack spoke.

00:15:49.017 --> 00:15:53.650
Did you take money from the car of senior Cavallio?

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:55.120
He asked.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:58.262
Yes, I took the money.

00:15:58.322 --> 00:15:59.808
Said the criminal.

00:15:59.868 --> 00:16:01.132
Guilty.

00:16:01.192 --> 00:16:03.054
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:16:03.114 --> 00:16:05.195
Five years in prison.

00:16:05.255 --> 00:16:07.236
Next criminal.

00:16:07.296 --> 00:16:11.238
The next criminal sat in the truth speaker's chair.

00:16:11.298 --> 00:16:16.662
Did you take diamonds from the house of Senorita Regia?

00:16:16.722 --> 00:16:18.853
Asked Inspector Sack.

00:16:18.914 --> 00:16:21.135
Yes, I did.

00:16:21.195 --> 00:16:22.626
Said the criminal.

00:16:22.686 --> 00:16:23.897
Guilty.

00:16:23.957 --> 00:16:25.548
Shouted the Inspector.

00:16:25.608 --> 00:16:27.749
Ten years in prison.

00:16:27.809 --> 00:16:30.752
Next criminal.

00:16:30.812 --> 00:16:34.296
The next criminal came in.

00:16:34.356 --> 00:16:37.148
He sat in the truth-speaker's chair.

00:16:37.208 --> 00:16:41.002
Did you kill Senor Ray?

00:16:41.062 --> 00:16:43.244
Asked Inspector Sack.

00:16:43.304 --> 00:16:45.676
The criminal was silent.

00:16:45.736 --> 00:16:47.808
Then he spoke.

00:16:47.868 --> 00:16:50.580
Yes, I did.

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:52.131
He said.

00:16:52.191 --> 00:16:54.342
That was the truth.

00:16:54.402 --> 00:16:55.844
Guilty!

00:16:55.904 --> 00:16:57.646
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:16:57.706 --> 00:16:59.458
Twenty years.

00:16:59.517 --> 00:17:00.937
Next.

00:17:00.997 --> 00:17:04.497
All the criminals sat in the truth-speaker's chair.

00:17:04.557 --> 00:17:06.627
They all told the truth.

00:17:06.688 --> 00:17:08.998
One of them was innocent.

00:17:09.058 --> 00:17:13.150
You are not guilty, said Inspector Sack.

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:15.380
You can go home.

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:18.111
Inspector Sack was pleased.

00:17:18.171 --> 00:17:20.332
Professor Verity was pleased.

00:17:20.392 --> 00:17:22.862
The Chief Inspector was pleased.

00:17:22.923 --> 00:17:24.813
Good work, Sack!

00:17:24.873 --> 00:17:26.554
Said the Chief Inspector.

00:17:26.614 --> 00:17:28.624
Very good work.

00:17:28.684 --> 00:17:30.452
Thank you, sir.

00:17:30.512 --> 00:17:32.261
said Inspector Sack.

00:17:32.321 --> 00:17:34.792
We are fighting crime, sir.

00:17:34.853 --> 00:17:37.204
The throat machine is helping us.

00:17:37.264 --> 00:17:41.016
There are no more criminals for us, sir."

00:17:41.076 --> 00:17:43.358
Inspector Sack smiled.

00:17:43.418 --> 00:17:44.928
He was happy.

00:17:44.988 --> 00:17:47.650
Yes, Inspector Sack.

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.642
No more criminals.

00:17:49.702 --> 00:17:52.044
No more work.

00:17:52.104 --> 00:17:55.576
No more work for me, sir?

00:17:55.636 --> 00:17:56.916
Yes.

00:17:56.976 --> 00:18:00.265
We don't need you now, Inspector Sack.

00:18:00.325 --> 00:18:02.564
I haven't got a job.

00:18:02.624 --> 00:18:06.507
What shall I do now?"

00:18:06.567 --> 00:18:10.440
It was Monday evening.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.323
Dr. Simple came to the laboratory.

00:18:13.383 --> 00:18:15.505
Another man came with him.

00:18:15.565 --> 00:18:18.117
The other man was a spy.

00:18:18.178 --> 00:18:20.309
Good evening, Professor.

00:18:20.369 --> 00:18:22.090
Said Dr. Simple.

00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:24.232
Good evening, Dr. Simple.

00:18:24.292 --> 00:18:25.703
Said the Professor.

00:18:25.764 --> 00:18:27.652
Everything is ready.

00:18:27.712 --> 00:18:30.071
"'Good,' said Dr. Simple.

00:18:30.091 --> 00:18:32.513
"'This spy is dangerous.

00:18:32.533 --> 00:18:33.994
"'He is an enemy.

00:18:34.014 --> 00:18:36.076
"'I will be his questioner.

00:18:36.096 --> 00:18:37.937
"'He will be the truth speaker.

00:18:37.957 --> 00:18:40.840
"'He will tell the truth.'"

00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:43.872
The professor went to the controls.

00:18:43.932 --> 00:18:46.804
Dr. Simple sat in the questioner's chair.

00:18:46.864 --> 00:18:49.166
The spy sat in the truth speaker's chair.

00:18:49.186 --> 00:18:51.979
"'What is your name?'

00:18:52.039 --> 00:18:53.866
asked Dr. Simple.

00:18:53.926 --> 00:18:58.644
My name is Harville Lime, said the spy.

00:18:58.704 --> 00:19:00.586
Where are you from?

00:19:00.646 --> 00:19:02.478
asked Dr. Simple.

00:19:02.538 --> 00:19:06.310
I am from Russia, said the spy.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.422
The spy smiled.

00:19:08.482 --> 00:19:10.913
Dr. Simple looked at the professor.

00:19:10.973 --> 00:19:13.224
Dr. Simple was pleased.

00:19:13.284 --> 00:19:17.278
Excellent, Professor Verity, said Dr. Simple.

00:19:17.338 --> 00:19:19.268
Lime is telling the truth.

00:19:19.328 --> 00:19:21.690
He will tell me everything.

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:25.646
Professor Verity was happy.

00:19:25.706 --> 00:19:28.730
Dr. Simple looked at Lime.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:32.611
�Are you a spy?� he asked.

00:19:32.631 --> 00:19:36.453
�Yes, I am a spy.

00:19:36.513 --> 00:19:40.594
I am an important spy,� said Lime.

00:19:40.654 --> 00:19:46.412
�Do you know the secret of the new military aircraft?� he asked.

00:19:46.472 --> 00:19:48.939
How the lime smiled.

00:19:48.999 --> 00:19:51.560
Yes, he said.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:58.584
I know the secret of the new military aircraft, and my government knows, too.

00:19:58.644 --> 00:19:59.955
Ah!

00:20:00.015 --> 00:20:01.616
cried Dr. Simple.

00:20:01.676 --> 00:20:04.267
The truth's machine is wonderful.

00:20:04.327 --> 00:20:07.048
This spy is telling me everything.

00:20:07.108 --> 00:20:11.400
But I have another secret, said lime.

00:20:11.461 --> 00:20:13.592
He looked at Dr. Simple.

00:20:13.652 --> 00:20:16.111
He looked at Professor Verity.

00:20:16.171 --> 00:20:29.698
Another secret cried dr. Simple tell me tell me tell me the truth My secret is this said how the line I Never tell the truth.

