00:27:51.048 --> 00:28:01.060
Chapter 1 A new start for Max.

00:28:01.120 --> 00:28:11.082
Max Price was a happy man.

00:28:11.142 --> 00:28:16.286
He loved his wife Angela and his two children, Stephen and Juliet.

00:28:16.346 --> 00:28:20.208
Max and his family lived in a small, pleasant flat.

00:28:20.268 --> 00:28:23.739
They had many good friends and kind neighbors.

00:28:23.799 --> 00:28:27.712
Yes, the Price family was a happy family.

00:28:27.772 --> 00:28:31.504
But one day, Max lost his job.

00:28:31.564 --> 00:28:34.025
The bad news came in a letter.

00:28:34.085 --> 00:28:36.550
The letter was short and clear.

00:28:36.610 --> 00:28:39.307
Max became very worried.

00:28:39.367 --> 00:28:41.449
What shall I do now?

00:28:41.509 --> 00:28:43.330
He said to his wife.

00:28:43.390 --> 00:28:45.542
I don't know, Max.

00:28:45.602 --> 00:28:48.384
I don't know, replied Angela.

00:28:48.444 --> 00:28:52.108
She was very worried, too.

00:28:52.168 --> 00:28:56.010
Then Max became angry.

00:28:56.070 --> 00:28:58.502
Look at this letter, he said.

00:28:58.562 --> 00:29:00.794
They send me best wishes.

00:29:00.855 --> 00:29:02.926
I don't want best wishes.

00:29:02.986 --> 00:29:04.278
I want a job.

00:29:04.338 --> 00:29:06.952
I've got a wife and family.

00:29:07.012 --> 00:29:10.246
Don't worry, Max," said Angela.

00:29:10.306 --> 00:29:12.558
Everything will be all right.

00:29:12.618 --> 00:29:15.900
But who will give me a job now, Angela?

00:29:15.960 --> 00:29:20.564
I'm 37, and today 37 is old.

00:29:20.624 --> 00:29:23.116
What are we going to do?

00:29:23.176 --> 00:29:27.788
Let's ask our friends and neighbors, said Angela.

00:29:27.848 --> 00:29:31.360
But they got no help from their friends and neighbors.

00:29:31.421 --> 00:29:33.912
Many people were looking for jobs.

00:29:33.972 --> 00:29:36.954
Life was difficult for everybody.

00:29:37.014 --> 00:29:40.336
Every morning Max looked for a new job.

00:29:40.396 --> 00:29:43.818
Every afternoon, he came home without one.

00:29:43.878 --> 00:29:49.652
And every evening, he waited for the newspaper.

00:29:49.712 --> 00:29:56.986
Will there be a job tonight?

00:29:57.046 --> 00:30:00.788
Hm.

00:30:00.848 --> 00:30:02.038
Jobs.

00:30:02.098 --> 00:30:03.809
Situations vacant.

00:30:03.869 --> 00:30:07.314
Twelve to fourteen.

00:30:07.374 --> 00:30:11.588
Nothing here again.

00:30:11.648 --> 00:30:18.010
Angela, look at this.

00:30:18.070 --> 00:30:22.512
The sky's the limit.

00:30:22.572 --> 00:30:26.873
Join our new company and go to the top.

00:30:26.933 --> 00:30:35.746
Friendly people, good salaries, jobs for men and women of all ages, the star building city center.

00:30:35.806 --> 00:30:38.980
Interviews every morning at nine.

00:30:39.040 --> 00:30:42.754
Mr. Lele, personnel manager.

00:30:42.815 --> 00:30:49.416
Friendship Services International, Star Building, City Center.

00:30:49.476 --> 00:30:53.947
Friendship Services International.

00:30:54.007 --> 00:30:56.828
It's a new company, said Max.

00:30:56.888 --> 00:30:59.238
What do you think, Angela?

00:30:59.298 --> 00:31:02.249
Go and see them, said Angela.

00:31:02.309 --> 00:31:08.338
They need new people, men and women, and all ages, too.

00:31:08.398 --> 00:31:10.937
Yes, said Max.

00:31:10.997 --> 00:31:13.118
The star building.

00:31:13.178 --> 00:31:16.289
That's the new skyscraper in the city center.

00:31:16.350 --> 00:31:18.660
It's a big company, Angela.

00:31:18.720 --> 00:31:20.392
Very big.

00:31:20.452 --> 00:31:23.843
You can go in the morning, said Angela.

00:31:23.903 --> 00:31:26.014
I will, said Max.

00:31:26.074 --> 00:31:27.614
He was excited.

00:31:27.674 --> 00:31:29.446
I'll be there early.

00:31:29.506 --> 00:31:31.916
I'll be there at seven o'clock.

00:31:31.976 --> 00:31:33.938
I'll get a job, Angela.

00:31:33.998 --> 00:31:35.860
Don't worry.

00:31:35.920 --> 00:31:40.183
Early next morning, Max was at the star building.

00:31:40.243 --> 00:31:46.545
At nine o'clock, he had an interview with three men from Friendship Services International.

00:31:46.605 --> 00:31:49.656
What was your last job?

00:31:49.716 --> 00:31:52.717
asked Mr. Lele, the personnel manager.

00:31:52.777 --> 00:31:55.898
I sold furniture, said Max.

00:31:55.958 --> 00:32:02.355
We don't need furniture salesman here, said the second man, Mr. Creep.

00:32:02.415 --> 00:32:05.541
"'But I'll learn a new job,' said Max quickly.

00:32:05.561 --> 00:32:07.412
"'I'll work hard.'"

00:32:07.472 --> 00:32:10.623
"'Good,' said the third man, Mr. Heitauer.

00:32:10.643 --> 00:32:18.406
"'We need new man, and we need hard workers, Mr. Price,' said Max quickly.

00:32:18.426 --> 00:32:22.207
"'Very good, Price,' said Mr. Heitauer.

00:32:22.227 --> 00:32:25.048
"'Be here tomorrow at 8.30.

00:32:25.108 --> 00:32:30.070
We are now working for friendship services internationally.

00:32:30.130 --> 00:32:32.922
Now Max had a job.

00:32:32.982 --> 00:32:35.885
He ran home and told Angela the good news.

00:32:35.945 --> 00:32:50.417
This was a new start for Max.

00:32:50.477 --> 00:33:04.226
Chapter 2 The Ground Floor The next day, Max went to his new job.

00:33:04.286 --> 00:33:07.880
His office was on the ground floor of the star building.

00:33:07.940 --> 00:33:10.642
Many new people started work that day.

00:33:10.702 --> 00:33:12.964
One of them was Frank Stedman.

00:33:13.024 --> 00:33:15.586
He became Max's friend.

00:33:15.646 --> 00:33:21.050
Their office was large and busy, but everybody was very friendly.

00:33:21.110 --> 00:33:26.116
Max and Frank liked everybody, and they did their work well.

00:33:26.176 --> 00:33:29.809
I like it here, Max," said Frank one day.

00:33:29.869 --> 00:33:33.690
We've got good jobs at Friendship Services International.

00:33:33.750 --> 00:33:35.590
Yes, said Max.

00:33:35.650 --> 00:33:37.650
I like it here, too.

00:33:37.710 --> 00:33:40.631
So the two men were very happy.

00:33:40.691 --> 00:33:44.712
Every lunchtime they had drinks and sandwiches with their new friends.

00:33:44.772 --> 00:33:47.462
In the evenings they went to parties with them.

00:33:47.522 --> 00:33:51.613
Max and Frank often took their wives and children to the parties.

00:33:51.673 --> 00:33:56.120
Max was pleased, and Angela was pleased, too.

00:33:56.180 --> 00:34:03.491
Max now had a good salary, so he and Angela bought lots of new furniture for their flat.

00:34:03.552 --> 00:34:08.714
They bought a color television, a hi-fi, and many other things.

00:34:08.774 --> 00:34:13.958
Angela bought some new clothes, and the children had lots of new toys.

00:34:14.018 --> 00:34:16.440
The Price family was happy again.

00:34:16.460 --> 00:34:19.162
"'You're rich!"

00:34:19.222 --> 00:34:21.628
said Angela, one day to Max.

00:34:21.688 --> 00:34:23.263
Max laughed.

00:34:23.323 --> 00:34:26.675
No, not yet, Angela, he said.

00:34:26.736 --> 00:34:29.988
But perhaps I'll be rich one day.

00:34:30.048 --> 00:34:34.152
Let's drink to your new job, said Angela.

00:34:34.212 --> 00:34:36.404
Yes, agreed Max.

00:34:36.464 --> 00:34:39.056
Let's drink to my new employer.

00:34:39.116 --> 00:34:42.920
Let's drink to friendship services international.

00:34:42.980 --> 00:34:44.700
Cheers, Angela.

00:34:44.761 --> 00:34:49.487
Cheers, Max, said Angela.

00:34:49.548 --> 00:34:55.194
The work at Friendship Services International was hard.

00:34:55.254 --> 00:34:59.126
Every day, Max and Frank received lots of letters.

00:34:59.186 --> 00:35:02.688
These letters wanted FSI products.

00:35:02.748 --> 00:35:06.099
But FSI products had no names.

00:35:06.159 --> 00:35:08.920
They only had numbers and letters.

00:35:08.980 --> 00:35:15.214
X3Ys, L7Ks, A5Qs.

00:35:15.274 --> 00:35:19.046
What did these strange numbers and letters mean?

00:35:19.106 --> 00:35:21.821
Max and Frank did not know.

00:35:21.881 --> 00:35:25.736
Each day they opened hundreds of these orders.

00:35:25.796 --> 00:35:35.682
They put the orders into groups, one group for X products, one group for L products, and one group for A products.

00:35:35.742 --> 00:35:39.163
The orders came from all over the world.

00:35:39.223 --> 00:35:42.284
Some of the orders were very big.

00:35:42.344 --> 00:35:47.184
We're working very hard, said Max, to Frank one day.

00:35:47.245 --> 00:35:49.574
Yes, replied Frank.

00:35:49.634 --> 00:35:53.456
Letters, letters, letters, hundreds of them.

00:35:53.516 --> 00:35:55.648
What do they mean, Max?

00:35:55.708 --> 00:35:57.418
What do they want?

00:35:57.478 --> 00:36:00.090
What are they asking for?

00:36:00.150 --> 00:36:03.312
I don't know, said Max.

00:36:03.372 --> 00:36:06.464
Don't ask so many questions, Frank.

00:36:06.524 --> 00:36:09.327
Okay, said Frank.

00:36:09.387 --> 00:36:11.288
Okay.

00:36:11.348 --> 00:36:16.452
Later that day, a memo came from their boss, Mr. B.

00:36:16.512 --> 00:36:18.270
Creeper.

00:36:18.330 --> 00:36:20.967
Confidential.

00:36:21.027 --> 00:36:28.149
Date July 1st from B creep to M price and F Stedman.

00:36:28.209 --> 00:36:31.139
Please see me now in my office.

00:36:31.199 --> 00:36:32.409
Fifth floor.

00:36:32.469 --> 00:36:37.560
Copy to M high tower.

00:36:37.620 --> 00:36:43.482
Please sit down gentlemen.

00:36:43.542 --> 00:36:47.956
I have some news for you.

00:36:48.016 --> 00:36:51.542
We like your work.

00:36:51.602 --> 00:36:54.944
You will be coming up to the fifth floor.

00:36:55.004 --> 00:36:56.966
Well done, Frank.

00:36:57.026 --> 00:36:58.927
Well done, Max.

00:36:58.947 --> 00:37:20.434
Chapter 3 The Fifth Floor Max and Frank now worked on the fifth floor.

00:37:20.495 --> 00:37:24.488
There were two other men and one secretary in their new office.

00:37:24.549 --> 00:37:26.620
The office was quiet.

00:37:26.681 --> 00:37:29.623
Its furniture was modern and expensive.

00:37:29.684 --> 00:37:33.547
The secretary had a dictaphone and an electric typewriter.

00:37:33.608 --> 00:37:36.493
The four men had large desks.

00:37:36.553 --> 00:37:40.889
One day, Max and Frank looked down on the street below.

00:37:40.949 --> 00:37:44.222
There was a lot of noise and traffic in the street.

00:37:44.282 --> 00:37:49.015
Max and Frank remembered their friends on the ground floor.

00:37:49.075 --> 00:37:52.668
They were good friends, said Frank.

00:37:52.728 --> 00:37:55.029
Yes, said Max.

00:37:55.090 --> 00:37:59.010
But now we've got new friends on the fifth floor.

00:37:59.070 --> 00:38:05.221
But, remember the parties and the friendship on the ground floor, said Frank?

00:38:05.282 --> 00:38:13.428
Yes, said Max, but Frank, the salaries on the fifth floor are better.

00:38:13.488 --> 00:38:17.692
Max now had more money.

00:38:17.752 --> 00:38:21.826
Let's buy a new house, he said to Angela.

00:38:21.886 --> 00:38:27.646
But I like it here, said Angela, and the children like it here too.

00:38:27.706 --> 00:38:30.374
But Angela said Max.

00:38:30.434 --> 00:38:34.427
I now work on the fifth floor at Friendship Services International.

00:38:34.487 --> 00:38:36.238
My salary is bigger.

00:38:36.298 --> 00:38:38.941
Fifth floor people don't live in flats.

00:38:39.001 --> 00:38:40.912
They live in houses."

00:38:40.973 --> 00:38:43.956
But Max said Angela.

00:38:44.016 --> 00:38:46.197
All our friends live here.

00:38:46.257 --> 00:38:48.710
And the children go to school here.

00:38:48.770 --> 00:38:51.601
And our flat is lovely now.

00:38:51.662 --> 00:38:54.024
Max became angry.

00:38:54.084 --> 00:38:56.770
We are going to move, Angela.

00:38:56.830 --> 00:39:00.174
We are going to move next week."

00:39:00.234 --> 00:39:03.436
All right, said Angela.

00:39:03.496 --> 00:39:08.558
She smiled, but she was unhappy.

00:39:08.618 --> 00:39:17.831
The next week Max and Angela moved to a new house, but Frank's dead man and his wife did not move.

00:39:17.891 --> 00:39:20.652
We like our flat, said Frank.

00:39:20.712 --> 00:39:24.750
All our friends are near us, and the children like their school.

00:39:24.810 --> 00:39:28.030
No, I shall not move, Max."

00:39:28.090 --> 00:39:31.773
Max said nothing.

00:39:31.833 --> 00:39:37.158
Max and Frank worked hard in their fifth floor office.

00:39:37.218 --> 00:39:41.982
They received orders to Friendship Services International and priced them.

00:39:42.042 --> 00:39:46.514
For example, there was an order for 5,000 M5Bs.

00:39:46.574 --> 00:39:49.443
The prices were in a book.

00:39:49.503 --> 00:40:01.576
One M5B cost $10, so 5,000 M5B's cost 5,000 times 10 equals $50,000.

00:40:01.636 --> 00:40:07.206
But Max and Frank still did not understand M5B.

00:40:07.266 --> 00:40:11.658
What's an M5B, asked Frank?

00:40:11.718 --> 00:40:17.226
I don't know, said Max.

00:40:17.286 --> 00:40:22.486
Now their boss was Mr. M.

00:40:22.546 --> 00:40:23.567
Hightower.

00:40:23.627 --> 00:40:27.250
His office was on the tenth floor of the star building.

00:40:27.310 --> 00:40:31.762
He came down every day at five o'clock and spoke to Max and Frank.

00:40:31.782 --> 00:40:37.666
"'Your work is excellent, gentlemen,' said Mr. Hightower one day.

00:40:37.726 --> 00:40:38.587
Excellent.

00:40:38.607 --> 00:40:41.789
"'Thank you, Mr. Hightower,' said Max.

00:40:41.809 --> 00:40:46.254
"'Call me Mort, please,' said Mr. Hightower.

00:40:46.314 --> 00:40:47.678
Thank you, Mort.

00:40:47.738 --> 00:40:49.850
I will," said Max.

00:40:49.910 --> 00:40:52.272
But Frank said nothing.

00:40:52.332 --> 00:40:55.734
One day, Mr. Heitauer came down early.

00:40:55.794 --> 00:40:58.826
Max and Frank were alone in their office.

00:40:58.886 --> 00:41:00.748
Anything wrong, Mort?

00:41:00.808 --> 00:41:02.760
Ask Max.

00:41:02.820 --> 00:41:04.482
No!

00:41:04.542 --> 00:41:05.753
Nothing is wrong!

00:41:05.773 --> 00:41:08.796
Good news, gentlemen.

00:41:08.856 --> 00:41:14.329
We are going to open a new department on the tenth floor.

00:41:14.389 --> 00:41:18.380
And you will be the bosses.

00:41:18.440 --> 00:41:20.481
Thanks, Mort.

00:41:20.541 --> 00:41:28.604
That's great news.

00:41:28.664 --> 00:41:36.628
Chapter Four.

00:41:36.688 --> 00:41:39.750
Higher and higher.

00:41:39.810 --> 00:41:44.354
The tenth floor office was large and comfortable.

00:41:44.414 --> 00:41:47.158
Max and Frank were the only two men in it.

00:41:47.219 --> 00:41:50.982
They had large desks and large telephones.

00:41:51.042 --> 00:41:52.902
There was a secretary too.

00:41:52.962 --> 00:41:55.704
She also had a large desk.

00:41:55.764 --> 00:41:59.978
One morning, Max and Frank looked down on the city below.

00:42:00.038 --> 00:42:02.028
It was a long way.

00:42:02.089 --> 00:42:05.931
The people and the cars were very small.

00:42:05.992 --> 00:42:09.614
It's very high, Frank, said Max.

00:42:09.674 --> 00:42:11.746
I like it up here.

00:42:11.806 --> 00:42:15.228
It's too high, Max," said Frank.

00:42:15.288 --> 00:42:17.479
I liked it on the ground floor.

00:42:17.539 --> 00:42:20.100
There's too much work up here.

00:42:20.160 --> 00:42:22.722
But we must work, said Max.

00:42:22.782 --> 00:42:25.243
This is Friendship Services International.

00:42:25.303 --> 00:42:26.834
It's a good company.

00:42:26.894 --> 00:42:28.975
We must work.

00:42:29.035 --> 00:42:31.786
Max worked very hard.

00:42:31.846 --> 00:42:35.609
He often worked late in the office.

00:42:35.669 --> 00:42:40.061
One evening, Max came home early.

00:42:40.121 --> 00:42:42.056
Angela was pleased.

00:42:42.116 --> 00:42:43.802
Hello, Max.

00:42:43.862 --> 00:42:45.542
You're early tonight.

00:42:45.602 --> 00:42:48.184
I'm cooking your favorite meal."

00:42:48.244 --> 00:42:51.316
I'm sorry, Angela, said Max.

00:42:51.376 --> 00:42:53.517
I must go out again in a few minutes.

00:42:53.577 --> 00:42:56.168
I've got an important business dinner."

00:42:56.228 --> 00:42:59.760
Oh, please stay," said Angela.

00:42:59.820 --> 00:43:05.318
I don't see you a lot these days, and the children don't see you at all.

00:43:05.378 --> 00:43:10.006
I'm sorry, Angela," said Max, but it's an important dinner.

00:43:10.067 --> 00:43:11.558
I must go.

00:43:11.618 --> 00:43:13.400
Good-bye.

00:43:13.460 --> 00:43:15.802
Good-bye, Max.

00:43:15.862 --> 00:43:18.194
Good luck.

00:43:18.254 --> 00:43:22.028
Oh, Max thought Angela to herself.

00:43:22.088 --> 00:43:27.042
You are becoming a different man, and the children don't know you now.

00:43:27.102 --> 00:43:30.114
You are a stranger in our home.

00:43:30.174 --> 00:43:33.286
It was a very important business dinner.

00:43:33.346 --> 00:43:35.326
Max and Frank were there.

00:43:35.386 --> 00:43:42.708
They met many foreign customers of Friendship Services International, but Mort Heitauer wasn't at the dinner.

00:43:42.768 --> 00:43:44.979
Where's Heitauer tonight?

00:43:45.039 --> 00:43:46.419
Asked Frank.

00:43:46.479 --> 00:43:47.839
What?

00:43:47.899 --> 00:43:50.020
I don't know, said Max.

00:43:50.080 --> 00:43:52.110
He wasn't well this morning.

00:43:52.170 --> 00:43:54.921
He left the office early.

00:43:54.981 --> 00:43:58.670
Max and Frank talked to the dinner guests.

00:43:58.730 --> 00:44:01.110
came from all over the world.

00:44:01.170 --> 00:44:02.331
They were rich.

00:44:02.391 --> 00:44:04.932
They ate and drank a lot.

00:44:04.993 --> 00:44:10.676
We like friendship services internationally, said an African guest.

00:44:10.736 --> 00:44:15.770
Yes, your products are very good, said an Asian guest.

00:44:15.830 --> 00:44:18.071
Then Max asked a question.

00:44:18.131 --> 00:44:20.612
He spoke to an American guest.

00:44:20.672 --> 00:44:23.314
Excuse me, he said.

00:44:23.375 --> 00:44:26.771
Yes, said the American.

00:44:26.831 --> 00:44:30.737
I've read your letters to FSI, said Max.

00:44:30.797 --> 00:44:32.438
I've seen your orders.

00:44:32.498 --> 00:44:36.849
For example, you ordered 300 S-6Ts.

00:44:36.909 --> 00:44:40.190
That's right, said the American.

00:44:40.250 --> 00:44:42.661
300 S-6Ts.

00:44:42.721 --> 00:44:44.742
They were excellent.

00:44:44.802 --> 00:44:50.303
But what is S-6T, asked Max?

00:44:50.363 --> 00:44:52.764
What your orders mean?

00:44:52.824 --> 00:44:55.114
I don't understand them.

00:44:55.174 --> 00:44:57.439
The American laughs.

00:44:57.499 --> 00:44:58.884
Oh!

00:44:58.944 --> 00:45:00.866
Our orders!

00:45:00.926 --> 00:45:02.648
Don't worry.

00:45:02.708 --> 00:45:05.421
He said, you're learning one day.

00:45:05.441 --> 00:45:08.354
But not now, Max.

00:45:08.414 --> 00:45:11.557
The other guests laughed too.

00:45:11.617 --> 00:45:15.191
Max and Frank were going to ask another question.

00:45:15.251 --> 00:45:21.449
But at that moment, there was an urgent message for Max.

00:45:21.509 --> 00:45:26.944
From FSI headquarters.

00:45:27.004 --> 00:45:28.806
High tower dead.

00:45:28.866 --> 00:45:31.187
Move to his job tomorrow.

00:45:31.247 --> 00:45:33.828
Fifteenth floor.

00:45:33.888 --> 00:45:37.530
I've got Mort's job Frank.

00:45:37.591 --> 00:45:41.142
I'm on the fifteenth floor.

00:45:41.203 --> 00:45:43.764
Oh Max.

00:45:43.824 --> 00:45:51.640
Be careful.

00:45:51.700 --> 00:46:08.150
Chapter 5 An Important Man The office on the 15th floor had every modern office machine.

00:46:08.210 --> 00:46:13.914
There was also a beautiful carpet on the floor and modern paintings on the walls.

00:46:13.974 --> 00:46:18.176
Max didn't like the paintings, but they were expensive.

00:46:18.236 --> 00:46:20.548
That pleased Max.

00:46:20.609 --> 00:46:25.732
From the window, Max looked out at the other skyscrapers in the city.

00:46:25.792 --> 00:46:27.923
Yes, thought Max.

00:46:27.983 --> 00:46:30.374
I'm an important man now.

00:46:30.434 --> 00:46:33.286
I'm rising higher in FSI.

00:46:33.346 --> 00:46:36.108
I'm rising higher in the star building.

00:46:36.168 --> 00:46:39.160
And I've got a beautiful secretary.

00:46:39.220 --> 00:46:40.891
It was true.

00:46:40.951 --> 00:46:44.424
Max's secretary was called Donna Lott.

00:46:44.484 --> 00:46:46.544
She was beautiful.

00:46:46.604 --> 00:46:48.286
She liked Max.

00:46:48.346 --> 00:46:50.087
And Max liked her.

00:46:50.147 --> 00:46:52.656
They did a lot of work together.

00:46:52.716 --> 00:46:55.806
Max and Donna often worked late.

00:46:55.866 --> 00:46:59.027
Sometimes they went to restaurants after work.

00:46:59.088 --> 00:47:03.621
One evening, Max telephoned Angela from a restaurant.

00:47:03.682 --> 00:47:06.784
Hello, Angela, darling, you said.

00:47:06.844 --> 00:47:08.626
It's Max here.

00:47:08.686 --> 00:47:11.298
Max, said Angela.

00:47:11.358 --> 00:47:12.900
Where are you?

00:47:12.960 --> 00:47:14.782
We're waiting for you.

00:47:14.842 --> 00:47:17.124
It's nine o'clock.

00:47:17.184 --> 00:47:19.946
I'm in the office, said Max.

00:47:20.006 --> 00:47:21.578
I'm working late.

00:47:21.638 --> 00:47:24.500
But Max, said Angela.

00:47:24.560 --> 00:47:26.611
It's Steven's birthday.

00:47:26.671 --> 00:47:29.022
He's waiting for you.

00:47:29.082 --> 00:47:31.844
Oh, said Max.

00:47:31.904 --> 00:47:33.715
I forgot.

00:47:33.775 --> 00:47:35.816
I'm sorry, Angela.

00:47:35.876 --> 00:47:37.868
I'll see him tomorrow.

00:47:37.928 --> 00:47:41.540
Tomorrow, Max, said Angela.

00:47:41.600 --> 00:47:42.791
Tomorrow?

00:47:42.811 --> 00:47:45.222
Oh, Max.

00:47:45.282 --> 00:47:48.966
Your work is more important to you than your home.

00:47:49.026 --> 00:47:51.239
Angela was angry.

00:47:51.299 --> 00:47:53.460
She put the phone down.

00:47:53.520 --> 00:47:55.512
Max rang her again.

00:47:55.572 --> 00:48:00.044
But Angela did not answer.

00:48:00.105 --> 00:48:04.927
Max did not see his son the next day.

00:48:04.987 --> 00:48:06.688
He went to work early.

00:48:06.748 --> 00:48:08.650
There were many letters for him.

00:48:08.710 --> 00:48:11.622
Max and Donna worked hard.

00:48:11.682 --> 00:48:14.563
Do you understand these letters?

00:48:14.623 --> 00:48:16.658
Max asked Donna.

00:48:16.718 --> 00:48:18.932
What do you mean, Max?"

00:48:18.992 --> 00:48:20.472
she replied.

00:48:20.533 --> 00:48:24.444
Do you understand these orders, said Max?

00:48:24.504 --> 00:48:27.646
What is a B5R?

00:48:27.706 --> 00:48:30.507
What is a G9Q?

00:48:30.568 --> 00:48:31.568
Do you know?

00:48:31.588 --> 00:48:35.320
Donna spoke slowly.

00:48:35.380 --> 00:48:39.232
They're secret things, she said.

00:48:39.292 --> 00:48:41.683
I know, said Max.

00:48:41.743 --> 00:48:44.216
But why are they secret?

00:48:44.276 --> 00:48:47.930
I don't know, Max," said Donna.

00:48:47.991 --> 00:48:50.052
Then she smiled.

00:48:50.112 --> 00:48:52.614
But you can find out.

00:48:52.674 --> 00:48:53.926
How?

00:48:53.986 --> 00:48:55.137
asked Max.

00:48:55.197 --> 00:48:57.318
How can I find out?

00:48:57.379 --> 00:49:02.504
You can become a director of the company, said Donna.

00:49:02.564 --> 00:49:04.284
Max laughed.

00:49:04.344 --> 00:49:05.576
Me?

00:49:05.636 --> 00:49:07.398
Max Price?

00:49:07.458 --> 00:49:11.110
A director of Friendship Services International?

00:49:11.170 --> 00:49:13.391
It's impossible.

00:49:13.452 --> 00:49:16.982
It isn't impossible, said Donna.

00:49:17.042 --> 00:49:19.103
I can help you.

00:49:19.163 --> 00:49:21.604
You, said Max?

00:49:21.664 --> 00:49:23.405
He was surprised.

00:49:23.465 --> 00:49:26.616
How can you help me?

00:49:26.676 --> 00:49:29.227
I have a cousin.

00:49:29.287 --> 00:49:32.538
He is a director of FSI.

00:49:32.598 --> 00:49:35.460
But will he help me, Donna?

00:49:35.520 --> 00:49:36.850
Yes.

00:49:36.910 --> 00:49:39.291
Of course he'll help you, Max.

00:49:39.351 --> 00:49:42.034
You'll be a director, too.

00:49:42.094 --> 00:49:44.257
Thanks, Donna.

00:49:44.317 --> 00:49:56.723
Thanks a lot.

00:49:56.783 --> 00:50:05.478
Chapter 6 Bad news, good news.

00:50:05.538 --> 00:50:11.882
A few months later, Max became a director of Friendship Services International.

00:50:11.942 --> 00:50:14.222
He went to his first board meeting.

00:50:14.282 --> 00:50:17.653
It was on the twentieth floor of the star building.

00:50:17.713 --> 00:50:20.204
Max did not know the other men there.

00:50:20.264 --> 00:50:24.045
They were talking about sales and profits.

00:50:24.105 --> 00:50:28.596
"'X-5B's are selling well,' said one man.

00:50:28.616 --> 00:50:35.188
"'And we're making good profits on B3Q's,' said another man.

00:50:35.248 --> 00:50:37.824
Max looked at his papers.

00:50:37.884 --> 00:50:45.344
C-70s are selling well, he said, and we're making good profits on U-80s.

00:50:45.404 --> 00:50:47.864
Thank you, said somebody.

00:50:47.924 --> 00:50:50.366
Thank you, Mr. Price.

00:50:50.426 --> 00:50:52.937
Everybody smiled at Max.

00:50:52.997 --> 00:50:55.158
Max smiled at everybody.

00:50:55.218 --> 00:50:58.190
But Max still did not understand.

00:50:58.250 --> 00:51:05.733
C-70s and U-80s were selling well, but what were they?

00:51:05.793 --> 00:51:08.204
Max didn't know.

00:51:08.264 --> 00:51:11.044
Now Max was very busy.

00:51:11.104 --> 00:51:14.286
He always arrived home very late.

00:51:14.346 --> 00:51:17.447
One evening he arrived home about midnight.

00:51:17.508 --> 00:51:19.438
He was very tired.

00:51:19.498 --> 00:51:22.440
But Angela and the children were not there.

00:51:22.500 --> 00:51:25.152
Max looked in all the rooms.

00:51:25.212 --> 00:51:27.282
There was nobody.

00:51:27.342 --> 00:51:28.753
Angela!

00:51:28.813 --> 00:51:30.074
shouted Max.

00:51:30.134 --> 00:51:31.644
Where are you?

00:51:31.705 --> 00:51:32.895
Stephen!

00:51:32.956 --> 00:51:34.046
Juliet!

00:51:34.106 --> 00:51:35.336
Where are you?

00:51:35.397 --> 00:51:36.788
I'm home!

00:51:36.848 --> 00:51:38.660
It's Daddy!

00:51:38.720 --> 00:51:41.094
But there was no answer.

00:51:41.154 --> 00:51:43.835
Max went into the bedroom again.

00:51:43.896 --> 00:51:45.788
Then he found a letter.

00:51:45.848 --> 00:51:47.628
It was on the bed.

00:51:47.688 --> 00:51:50.130
Max looked at the envelope.

00:51:50.190 --> 00:51:52.612
Suddenly he felt sad.

00:51:52.672 --> 00:51:54.644
Suddenly he knew.

00:51:54.705 --> 00:51:58.208
He opened the envelope and read the letter.

00:51:58.268 --> 00:52:02.131
Yes, it was from Angela.

00:52:02.191 --> 00:52:07.270
Dear Max, I'm going away with the children.

00:52:07.330 --> 00:52:09.036
Good-bye, Max.

00:52:09.096 --> 00:52:10.706
We will think of you.

00:52:10.766 --> 00:52:12.237
Good-bye.

00:52:12.297 --> 00:52:15.118
All my love, Angela.

00:52:15.178 --> 00:52:16.469
P.S.

00:52:16.529 --> 00:52:20.650
Good luck on the board of directors."

00:52:20.710 --> 00:52:25.052
Now Max had no family.

00:52:25.112 --> 00:52:28.900
He was sad and lonely, so he traveled.

00:52:28.960 --> 00:52:32.246
He traveled for Friendship Services International.

00:52:32.306 --> 00:52:39.950
He traveled all over the five continents, Europe, Africa, Asia, America, Australia.

00:52:40.011 --> 00:52:42.362
Max was very good at his work.

00:52:42.422 --> 00:52:44.452
His customers liked him.

00:52:44.513 --> 00:52:48.164
Max took letters and papers to each customer.

00:52:48.225 --> 00:52:51.038
Many of the customers were scientists.

00:52:51.098 --> 00:52:53.992
The papers were top secret.

00:52:54.053 --> 00:52:56.373
Max did not understand them.

00:52:56.434 --> 00:52:58.634
He was not a scientist.

00:52:58.694 --> 00:53:02.657
He showed the papers to customers in many foreign countries.

00:53:02.717 --> 00:53:04.928
The customers read the documents.

00:53:04.988 --> 00:53:07.109
Then they made decisions.

00:53:07.169 --> 00:53:12.592
For example, one African scientist said, Thank you, Mr. Price.

00:53:12.652 --> 00:53:14.763
Thank you for the papers.

00:53:14.823 --> 00:53:16.862
They are very interesting.

00:53:16.922 --> 00:53:24.304
I shall order 15 S3Bs and 400 M2Gs."

00:53:24.364 --> 00:53:27.948
So Max was very popular with the other directors.

00:53:27.968 --> 00:53:32.792
"'Excellent work, Max," said the finance director one day.

00:53:32.812 --> 00:53:36.875
"'Yes, excellent," said the company's vice-chairman.

00:53:36.895 --> 00:53:43.359
"'We have a surprise for you, Max."

00:53:43.419 --> 00:53:48.707
You are now the chairman of FSI.

00:53:48.767 --> 00:53:50.430
Me?

00:53:50.490 --> 00:54:02.930
The chairman of FSI?

00:54:02.990 --> 00:54:22.828
CHAPTER VII THE SKY'S THE LIMIT Now Max was the chairman of Friendship Services International.

00:54:22.888 --> 00:54:26.590
Now he was at the top of the star building.

00:54:26.650 --> 00:54:30.311
His office was on the twenty-fifth floor.

00:54:30.371 --> 00:54:32.992
It was a very strange office.

00:54:33.052 --> 00:54:35.803
It was a very large white room.

00:54:35.863 --> 00:54:39.054
There was a big desk and one chair.

00:54:39.114 --> 00:54:42.110
On the desk there were two telephones.

00:54:42.170 --> 00:54:44.936
One telephone had the letter M on it.

00:54:44.996 --> 00:54:47.608
The other telephone had the letter W.

00:54:47.668 --> 00:54:53.183
Max said to himself, what are these phones for?

00:54:53.244 --> 00:54:55.416
But he did not know.

00:54:55.476 --> 00:54:58.518
There was a very large window in the office.

00:54:58.578 --> 00:55:02.542
From the window Max looked out at the clear blue sky.

00:55:02.602 --> 00:55:06.856
He remembered the Friendship Service's international advertisement.

00:55:06.916 --> 00:55:09.470
The sky's the limit.

00:55:09.530 --> 00:55:15.049
He remembered the interview with Mr. Lele, Mr. Creep, and Mort Heitauer.

00:55:15.110 --> 00:55:18.143
Then he thought about Frank Stedman.

00:55:18.203 --> 00:55:21.568
Where's Frank now, Max thought?

00:55:21.628 --> 00:55:23.970
But Max did not know.

00:55:24.030 --> 00:55:29.196
And Max remembered his wife, Angela, and his children, Stephen and Juliet.

00:55:29.256 --> 00:55:31.478
They never came back.

00:55:31.538 --> 00:55:35.079
Every evening Max went home to an empty house.

00:55:35.139 --> 00:55:37.920
But now his beautiful home was dirty.

00:55:37.980 --> 00:55:39.892
Nobody visited Max.

00:55:39.952 --> 00:55:41.672
He had no friends.

00:55:41.732 --> 00:55:43.283
He was alone.

00:55:43.343 --> 00:55:45.304
He was unhappy.

00:55:45.364 --> 00:55:48.495
Every evening Max wrote a letter.

00:55:48.555 --> 00:55:51.306
Every letter was the same.

00:55:51.366 --> 00:55:55.788
My darling Angela, please come home.

00:55:55.848 --> 00:55:57.219
I need you.

00:55:57.279 --> 00:55:58.600
I love you.

00:55:58.660 --> 00:56:00.510
Please bring the children.

00:56:00.570 --> 00:56:02.130
I love them too.

00:56:02.190 --> 00:56:04.170
Where are you, Angela?

00:56:04.230 --> 00:56:06.232
Please come home.

00:56:06.292 --> 00:56:09.063
All my love, Max.

00:56:09.123 --> 00:56:12.305
Max put each letter into an envelope.

00:56:12.365 --> 00:56:16.878
On every envelope, Max wrote, to my darling Angela.

00:56:16.938 --> 00:56:19.860
Now there were nearly a hundred letters.

00:56:19.920 --> 00:56:22.792
They were all the same.

00:56:22.852 --> 00:56:27.965
Max was chairman of FSI, but he had no work.

00:56:28.025 --> 00:56:30.306
Every day he came to his office.

00:56:30.366 --> 00:56:33.355
But every day there was no work.

00:56:33.416 --> 00:56:37.956
One morning he found a large book on his desk.

00:56:38.016 --> 00:56:39.497
What's this?

00:56:39.557 --> 00:56:41.719
He asked himself.

00:56:41.779 --> 00:56:45.822
At that moment the M telephone rang.

00:56:45.882 --> 00:56:47.504
Max picked it up.

00:56:47.564 --> 00:56:52.628
A voice said, send us five hundred N-five B's immediately.

00:56:52.688 --> 00:56:55.350
He will find details in the catalog.

00:56:55.410 --> 00:56:57.121
But who are you?

00:56:57.181 --> 00:56:58.192
Asked Max.

00:56:58.252 --> 00:57:00.784
And what are N-five B's?

00:57:00.844 --> 00:57:02.355
Max waited.

00:57:02.415 --> 00:57:04.486
But there was no answer.

00:57:04.546 --> 00:57:07.026
The W telephone rang.

00:57:07.087 --> 00:57:08.598
Max picked it up.

00:57:08.658 --> 00:57:13.682
Another voice said, send us 500 N5Bs immediately.

00:57:13.742 --> 00:57:16.584
You will find details in the catalog.

00:57:16.644 --> 00:57:18.846
But who are you?

00:57:18.906 --> 00:57:20.448
Max asked again.

00:57:20.508 --> 00:57:23.340
And what are N5Bs?

00:57:23.400 --> 00:57:25.432
Again, Max waited.

00:57:25.492 --> 00:57:27.524
But there was no answer.

00:57:27.584 --> 00:57:30.029
He was now frightened.

00:57:30.089 --> 00:57:31.794
Who is M?"

00:57:31.854 --> 00:57:33.075
said Max.

00:57:33.135 --> 00:57:35.006
And who is W?

00:57:35.066 --> 00:57:37.099
And N5B.

00:57:37.159 --> 00:57:39.911
What is N5B?

00:57:39.972 --> 00:57:42.994
Max picked up the catalog on his desk.

00:57:43.054 --> 00:57:45.747
He opened it at N.

00:57:45.807 --> 00:57:48.989
N5B.

00:57:49.050 --> 00:57:50.260
N.

00:57:50.320 --> 00:57:51.842
Nuclear.

00:57:51.902 --> 00:57:53.064
5.

00:57:53.124 --> 00:57:54.474
Missile.

00:57:54.534 --> 00:57:55.646
B.

00:57:55.706 --> 00:57:57.486
Starblast.

00:57:57.546 --> 00:57:59.587
General information.

00:57:59.647 --> 00:58:02.990
One, for land, sea, or air.

00:58:03.050 --> 00:58:06.422
Two, instant kill.

00:58:06.482 --> 00:58:08.704
Oh, no.

00:58:08.764 --> 00:58:16.369
I'm selling missiles, guns, bombs.

00:58:16.429 --> 00:58:20.332
I didn't know.

00:58:20.392 --> 00:58:22.404
I didn't know.

00:58:22.464 --> 00:58:25.562
What shall I do?

